From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: retro98boy <retro98boy@qq.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 17:43:04 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: qcom: q6apm: start DisplayPort graphs at trigger

The early playback start added for the Odin 3 I2S amplifier also
applies to DisplayPort. The CPU DAI then starts the graph before
the codec DAI prepares the DisplayPort audio engine. The DSP rejects
the start.

Leave DisplayPort graph startup to the PCM trigger. This restores
the ordering from b54a38af7138 ("ASoC: qcom: q6apm-lpass-dai: move
graph start to trigger").

Signed-off-by: retro98boy <retro98boy@qq.com>
---
 sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6apm-lpass-dais.c | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6apm-lpass-dais.c b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6apm-lpass-dais.c
index 56a6b8ded782..8a5afd7e38fc 100644
--- a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6apm-lpass-dais.c
+++ b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6apm-lpass-dais.c
@@ -266,6 +266,13 @@ static int q6apm_lpass_dai_prepare(struct snd_pcm_substream *substream, struct s
 		goto err;
 	}
 
+	/* Start at trigger after the codec prepares the DisplayPort audio engine. */
+	switch (dai->id) {
+	case DISPLAY_PORT_RX_0:
+	case DISPLAY_PORT_RX_1 ... DISPLAY_PORT_RX_7:
+		return 0;
+	}
+
 	/*
 	 * aw88166 checks its PLL against BCLK at DAPM PRE_PMU, before the
 	 * PCM trigger; start the port here so BCLK is up in time. The
